  "content": {
    "id": "p17-challenge-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "The electrical resistance, $R$ ohms, in a wire is directly proportional to its length, $L$ m, and inversely proportional to the square of its diameter, $D$ m. A certain wire 100 m long with a diameter 0.4 mm has a resistance 1.4 ohms.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-challenge-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the equation connecting $R$, $L$ and $D$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$R=\\dfrac{2.24\\times10^{-9}L}{D^2}$, with $L$ and $D$ in metres.",
          "worked": "Since $R\\propto \\frac{L}{D^2}$, write $R=\\frac{kL}{D^2}$. Convert the given diameter: $0.4\\text{ mm}=0.0004\\text{ m}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}1.4&=\\frac{100k}{(0.0004)^2}\\\\k&=\\frac{1.4(0.0004)^2}{100}\\\\k&=2.24\\times10^{-9}\\\\R&=\\frac{2.24\\times10^{-9}L}{D^2}\\end{align*}$$\nHere $L$ and $D$ are measured in metres and $R$ in ohms.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-challenge-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the resistance (correct to one decimal place) of a wire of the same material if it is 150 m in length and has a diameter of 0.25 mm.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5.4\\ \\Omega$.",
          "worked": "The diameter is $0.25\\text{ mm}=0.00025\\text{ m}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}R&=\\frac{2.24\\times10^{-9}\\times150}{(0.00025)^2}\\\\R&=5.376\\ \\Omega\\\\R&\\approx5.4\\ \\Omega\\end{align*}$$\nThe resistance is $5.4\\ \\Omega$, correct to one decimal place.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 35
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-challenge-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "If the length and diameter are doubled, what is the effect on the resistance?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The resistance is halved.",
          "worked": "Using $R=\\frac{kL}{D^2}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}R_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{k(2L)}{(2D)^2}\\\\R_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac12\\frac{kL}{D^2}\\\\R_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac12R\\end{align*}$$\nThe resistance is halved.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-challenge-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "If the length is increased by 10% and the diameter is decreased by 5%, what is the percentage change on the resistance? (Give your answer correct to one decimal place.)",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p17-challenge-q1-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The resistance increases by 21.9%.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p17-challenge-q1-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Multiply the resistance by ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{1.10}{0.95^2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and compare with its original value.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The new length is $1.10L$ and the new diameter is $0.95D$.\n$$\\begin{align*}R_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{k(1.10L)}{(0.95D)^2}\\\\R_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{1.10}{0.95^2}R\\\\R_{\\mathrm{new}}&=\\frac{440}{361}R\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Percentage increase}&=\\left(\\frac{440}{361}-1\\right)\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage increase}&=\\frac{7900}{361}\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage increase}&\\approx21.9\\%\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      }
    ]
  },
